{"tool_name":"synaptome.db","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"synaptome.db","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/release/data/annotation/html/synaptome.db.html","license":"Artistic-2.0","summary":"Bioconductor package for synaptic proteomics data.","addition_date":"2023-11-07T14:20:19.181287Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:32:42.358804Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:synaptome.db","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"oksana.sorokina@ed.ac.uk","name":"Oksana Sorokina","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Anatoly Sorokin","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"J Douglas Armstrong","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Information extraction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3907"},{"term":"Query and retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0224"}]}],"name":"Synaptome.db","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioadv/vbac086","metadata":{"abstract":"Summary: The neuronal synapse is underpinned by a large and diverse proteome but the molecular evidence is spread across many primary datasets. These data were recently curated into a single dataset describing a landscape of \u223c8000 proteins found in studies of mammalian synapses. Here, we describe programmatic access to the dataset via the R/Bioconductor package Synaptome.db, which enables convenient and in-depth data analysis from within the Bioconductor environment. Synaptome.db allows users to obtain the respective gene information, e.g. subcellular localization, brain region, gene ontology, disease association and construct custom protein-protein interaction network models for gene sets and entire subcellular compartments.","authors":[{"name":"Armstrong J.D."},{"name":"Sorokin A."},{"name":"Sorokina O."}],"citationCount":2,"date":"2022-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics Advanc